```java
public static int longestStableRun(int[] readings) {
    return scanStable(readings, 0, 0, 0);
}
private static int scanStable(int[] a, int i, int run, int best) {
    if (i == a.length) return best;
    int next;
    if (a[i] < 0 || a[i] > 100) next = 0;
    else if (run > 0 && Math.abs(a[i] - a[i - 1]) <= 3) next = run + 1;
    else next = 1;
    return scanStable(a, i + 1, next, Math.max(best, next));
}
```

This uses one recursive call per reading, so a long array can exhaust the call stack.

public static int longestStableRun(int[] readings) {
    int best = 0;
    for (int start = 0; start < readings.length; start++) {
        if (readings[start] < 0 || readings[start] > 100) continue;
        int end = start;
        while (end + 1 < readings.length && readings[end + 1] >= 0 && readings[end + 1] <= 100
                && Math.abs(readings[end + 1] - readings[end]) <= 3) end++;
        best = Math.max(best, end - start + 1);
    }
    return best;
}

